9. 📏 What is Granularity in Data Warehousing?
Granularity refers to the level of detail or depth of information stored in a fact table in a data warehouse.
🔍 Granularity = “How detailed is the data?”
Fine-grained (High granularity) → Very detailed
→ One row per transaction, minute, customer, etc.

Coarse-grained (Low granularity) → Less detailed
→ One row per day, product category, or region

🎯 Why is Granularity Important?
Choosing the right granularity impacts:
🔄 Data size (storage cost)
⏱️ Query performance
📊 Analysis flexibility
🔧 ETL complexity
